<article class="env-lemma" id="0B78">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B78">Lemma <span data-tag="0B78">42.33.2</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a flat morphism of relative dimension $r$ between schemes locally of finite type over $S$. Then the rule that to $Y' \to Y$ assigns $(f')^* : \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(Y') \to \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _{k + r}(X')$ where $X' = X \times _ Y Y'$ is a bivariant class of degree $-r$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/02S1" data-tag="02S1">42.20.2</a>, <a href="/tag/02RD" data-tag="02RD">42.14.3</a>, <a href="/tag/02RG" data-tag="02RG">42.15.1</a>, and <a href="/tag/0B71" data-tag="0B71">42.29.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>